# Decision Records / Testing / DB Docs / Naming

Japanese human-facing sources of truth:

- Record the reason for a non-trivial decision next to the rule it shapes, in the owning doc (no separate decision-record directory)
- `docs/rules/testing.md` — behavior-changing source changes ship with colocated tests (`*_test.go` / `*.test.ts(x)`); frontend test granularity per `frontend/architecture.md` §8. CI `Test Presence` fails when an API operation has no Handler test / no generated-MSW-handler test, and warns when a changed source has no test change in the same directory. DB-backed tests fail (not skip) without PostgreSQL: `make db-up migrate-up` first
- `docs/rules/db-documentation.md` — `backend/migrations/*.sql` changes ship with `docs/db/backend-schema.{json,md}` updates; table names are singular snake_case business concepts
- `docs/rules/code-comments.md` — Why-not comments by default; one-line Japanese What doc comments for the listed types/functions
- Naming: backend `backend/architecture.md` §2 (`<Verb><Subject>Usecase`, `Read` for one item, `Search` for lists, Repository/Query `Find*` / `Search` / `Count*` / `Exists*`); frontend `frontend/architecture.md` §9
- Lint enforces: Go `gosec` / `modernize` / complexity ≤ 10 (`make lint`); TS `strict` + `stylistic` + `@eslint-react` + react-hooks recommended, no imports between features, no `../` imports, named exports only (`pnpm lint`)
